WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.648
Fluent spoken reading is clear, appropriately paced, accurate and expressive;

00:00:05.648 --> 00:00:07.283
self-correction supports understanding.

00:00:08.117 --> 00:00:12.912
What is the purpose of a full stop during oral reading? Answer: Pause and mark the

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.111
end of a sentence.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:19.932
Read a passage twice and record where your pacing, expression or pronunciation

00:00:19.932 --> 00:00:20.347
improved.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.824
Why it works: Pausing marks the sentence ending.
